{
  "evidence": "TEXT_G: Seek an agreed, legally watertight Section 30 process for an independence referendum; uphold the rules‑based international order; introduce an NHS Protection Act; support veterans while scrapping Trident and reinvesting in conventional defence; protect Scotland’s fishing interests with Scottish leadership in negotiations; tackle tax avoidance/evasion, enforce prompt payment, and strengthen fair work (ban exploitative zero‑hours, enforce gender pay gap standards); uprate benefits and scrap the two‑child cap; climate targets with a just transition and a Net Zero Fund. TEXT_C: Overhaul the constitution with proportional representation, an elected second chamber, citizens’ assemblies, and a People’s Constitution; halve the prison population and end the war on drugs via legal, regulated supply; cancel Trident and end arms sales; implement UBI, rent controls, and a higher Living Wage; impose a Land Value Tax, rising Carbon Tax, and a Frequent Flyer Levy; strong nature‑protection measures (Clean Air Act, ecocide law, rewilding, ending factory farming) and no new nuclear.",
  "reasoning": "Given high weights on authority and loyalty, TEXT_G leans more toward working through established legal channels and advancing in‑group commitments (veterans, Scottish sector interests) while also addressing equality and proportionality through fair work and anti‑avoidance measures. TEXT_C emphasizes systemic constitutional overhaul, reduced punitive authority, and a strong sanctity‑of‑nature and equality agenda, which fits lower‑weighted foundations better than the electorate’s top priorities.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_G"
}
